# L §2.3 calval (writer 8): calendar(weekends [...], yearly [...] [from Y], added [...]); the `removed` list is gone (a
# version replaces that year's row, L §4.2), so `removed [...]` doesn't parse: LOAD-PARSE.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input len: calendar

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2026-01-01
  len = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], removed [2026-01-01])

ask q: is_business(2026-01-02, len)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE ...
